        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/torah/before_blessing@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <tei:note type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n168.jpg" xml:lang="en">Then the reading of the Torah begins until the end of the portion when the individual who had been called upon, says:</tei:note>
        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/torah/after_blessing@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <tei:div>
          <tei:head xml:lang="en">Reading from the First Torah Scroll</tei:head>
          <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        </tei:div>
        <tei:note type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n172.jpg" xml:lang="en">The second scroll of the Torah is then placed next to the first on the reading desk and the Reader says half-kaddish. The first scroll is then raised and rolled together. After that, the second scroll is unrolled and someone is called to the reading for Maphtir which is taken from Pinhas.</tei:note>
        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:numbers/29/1-/29/6@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <tei:note type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n174.jpg" xml:lang="en">After the reading, the Torah scroll is lifted up and rolled together again. When the Torah scroll is being lifted up, one says:</tei:note>
        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:chol/shacharit/torah/vezot_hatorah@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <tei:note type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n174.jpg" xml:lang="en">Blessing before the Haphtorah:</tei:note>
        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/asher_bachar@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <tei:div>
          <tei:head xml:lang="en">Haphtarah</tei:head>
          <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:samuel_1/1/1-/2/10@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        </tei:div>
        <tei:note type="instruction" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n182.jpg" xml:lang="en">Blessings after the Haphtorah:</tei:note>
        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/after@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <j:transclude type="external" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkhot_haftarah/al_hatorah_festival@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>
        <tei:div>
          <tei:note type="instruction" xml:lang="en" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n182.jpg">After the Haphtora the Shofar is blown.<tei:seg type="optional-page-reference"> But when the first day of the festival falls on a Sabbath, then one continues immediately with <tei:foreign xml:lang="he">יקום פורקן</tei:foreign> (p. <tei:ref type="page" target="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yequm_purqan/scholars@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"/>)</tei:seg></tei:note>
        </tei:div>
        <tei:anchor xml:id="documentary_torah_draft_gap_en"/>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
